 safe he called his boss stud  manager gus lane drion who then tried to  read jayukah in switzerland a few other  people including shaggy's veterinarian a  finance minister and an official with  the irish thoroughbred breeding  association were all apprised of what  had happened and none of them were  really sure how to proceed high profile  whole snappings were quite rare the last  one had occurred in 1977 when a mare  named fran faloush was stolen from her  paddock in kentucky eventually one of  them we don't know who contacted the  police and told them what happened but  by then the gunman had at least a six  hour head start  [Music]  the next day local police started the  search for sureguard but the kidnappers  had picked their opportunity very  carefully a big horse sale was taking  place in the area that day so there were  a sea of horses and trailers everywhere  the criminals could have probably ridden  sugar down the street without anyone  noticing them plus from the very  beginning the investigation was hampered  by the fact that multiple law  enforcement agencies got involved and  they didn't play very nicely with each  other it soon became evident that they  had no choice but to wait for the ransom  call it came the next evening kiss  adrian the ballet money manager answered  the call and following instructions from  the garda the irish police service he  played dumb and stalled the time to keep  the kidnappers on the line for 90  seconds in order to trace the call or it  seems like the criminals had seen the  same police movies as the rest of us and  were wise to the trick they hung out the  phone and called back several times to  prevent a trace occasionally the  conversation turned to a surreal comedy  sketch as dreel a frenchman struggled to  understand the caller's thick irish  accent while the man on the other end  had the same problem with his french  accent eventually the kidnappers got fed  up with dreon and demanded to speak with  agar khan or 